@{
    ViewBag.Title = "Help";
}

<h1 class="th-section-header">Help</h1>

<div class="th-card">
    <h3 style="margin-top:0;">About</h3>
    <p>
        <strong>DataBank Unity API Test Harness (Web)</strong> is an ASP.NET MVC reproduction of Unity.TestHarness
        (the WPF version), matching its functionality, look, and feel. It exercises the Unity API library suite
        (Unity.00 through Unity.04) end to end: connecting with any of the four authentication modes, browsing the
        full taxonomy hierarchy, retrieving documents, and creating, updating, and deleting them.
    </p>
    <p>
        This project targets .NET Framework 4.8 as a legacy-style ASP.NET Web Application (classic ASP.NET has no
        official SDK-style support), matching the rest of the Unity training track.
    </p>
    <p class="th-text-secondary">Version: @ViewBag.AppVersion</p>
</div>

<div class="th-card">
    <h3 style="margin-top:0;">License and Support</h3>
    <p>
        This repository is provided under the <a href="#" id="th-license-link">MIT License</a>. You are free to
        use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell the materials in this repository,
        subject to the terms of that license.
    </p>
    <p>
        This repository is provided for training and reference purposes only. DataBank IMX does not provide
