    </p>
</div>

<h3>Instructions</h3>

<details class="th-card">
    <summary style="cursor:pointer; font-weight:600;">Connect</summary>
    <p style="margin-top:10px;">
        Configure a connection on the <a href="@Url.Action("Index", "Settings")">Settings</a> page first, then use
        Connect here.
    </p>
    <p>
        &bull; <strong>Connect</strong> establishes a session using whatever's currently configured (reconnects to a
        Session ID first if one's set, otherwise uses the configured Authentication Mode).<br />
        &bull; <strong>Reconnect to Session ID</strong> is a separate, ad hoc reconnect, independent of Settings.<br />
        &bull; <strong>Test API Availability</strong> pings the Application Server directly, bypassing the Unity API
        entirely. It runs automatically every time you visit this page.<br />
        &bull; A connected session is disconnected automatically on session expiration (browser tab closed without a
        manual Disconnect), a delayed safety net since a closed tab sends the server no signal at all.
    </p>
</details>

<details class="th-card">
    <summary style="cursor:pointer; font-weight:600;">Taxonomy</summary>
    <p style="margin-top:10px;">
        Click <strong>Load Taxonomy</strong> first (it connects automatically if needed).
    </p>
    <p>
        &bull; Browse the cascading hierarchy: select a Document Type Group to see its Document Types, select a
        Document Type to see its Keyword Group Types and Standalone Keywords, select a Keyword Group Type to see its
        own Keyword Types.<br />
        &bull; Custom Queries, File Types, and Unity Form Templates are separate, flat lookups alongside the
        hierarchy.
    </p>
</details>

<details class="th-card">
    <summary style="cursor:pointer; font-weight:600;">Retrieval</summary>
    <p style="margin-top:10px;">
        Three ways to find a document, chosen via the tabs at the top of Search Criteria:
    </p>
    <p>
        &bull; <strong>Document Type(s)</strong> &mdash; select one or more Document Types (optionally narrowed by a
        Group filter), fill in any keyword fields common to all of them, then Search.<br />
        &bull; <strong>Custom Query</strong> &mdash; select one query and fill in its own keyword fields.<br />
        &bull; <strong>Document ID</strong> &mdash; retrieves a single document directly, bypassing search entirely.
    </p>
    <p>
        Selecting a result loads its full detail below: metadata, keyword groups, and a Revisions/Renditions browser
        (defaulting to the first revision's first rendition). Use <strong>Retrieve File</strong> to download the
        selected rendition's file (check <strong>Prefer PDF</strong> to convert on the fly, where supported).
    </p>
</details>

<details class="th-card">
    <summary style="cursor:pointer; font-weight:600;">Archiving</summary>
    <p style="margin-top:10px;">
        Five modes, chosen via the tabs at the top:
    </p>
    <p>
        &bull; <strong>Store New</strong> &mdash; pick a Document Type, attach file(s) (drag/drop or browse), fill in
        keywords, then Store.<br />
        &bull; <strong>Modify Metadata</strong>, <strong>Add Revision</strong>, <strong>Add Rendition</strong>, and
        <strong>Delete</strong> all share one "load by Document ID" step. Add Revision/Add Rendition are only
        enabled when the loaded document's type actually supports them.<br />
        &bull; For keyword groups: a Multi-Instance group's <strong>+ Add Instance</strong>/<strong>Remove
        Instance</strong> lets you add or remove whole sets of that group's fields; a Single-Instance group is
        capped at exactly one. Any standalone keyword can independently have more than one value via its own
        <strong>+ Add Value</strong>/<strong>Remove</strong>.<br />
        &bull; <strong>Delete</strong>'s <strong>Purge</strong> checkbox (off by default) permanently purges the
        document rather than a regular, recoverable delete; both prompt for confirmation first.
    </p>
</details>

<details class="th-card">
    <summary style="cursor:pointer; font-weight:600;">Settings</summary>
    <p style="margin-top:10px;">
        Edits the connection configuration used everywhere else in the app. This is an admin-style, global setting
        &mdash; changes here affect every user of this app, not just you.
    </p>
    <p>
        &bull; <strong>Apply</strong> takes effect immediately, in memory, for this run only.<br />
        &bull; <strong>Save to Web.config</strong> also applies, then additionally writes to disk, so it persists
        across app pool recycles/restarts.
    </p>
</details>

<!-- License popup -->
<div id="th-license-modal" style="display:none; position:fixed; inset:0; background:rgba(0,0,0,0.5); z-index:1000; align-items:center; justify-content:center;">
    <div style="background:#fff; border-radius:var(--th-radius); max-width:640px; width:90%; max-height:80vh; display:flex; flex-direction:column; padding:24px;">
        <h3 style="margin-top:0;">License</h3>
        <div id="th-license-text" style="overflow-y:auto; flex:1; font-family:Consolas, monospace; font-size:12px; white-space:pre-wrap; background:var(--th-surface); border:1px solid var(--th-border); border-radius:var(--th-radius); padding:16px;"></div>
        <button type="button" id="th-license-close" class="th-btn th-btn-primary" style="margin-top:16px; align-self:flex-end;">Close</button>
    </div>
</div>

@section scripts {
    <script>
        (function () {
            var modal = document.getElementById('th-license-modal');
            var textEl = document.getElementById('th-license-text');

            document.getElementById('th-license-link').addEventListener('click', function (e) {
                e.preventDefault();
                fetch('@Url.Action("ShowLicense")')
                    .then(function (r) { return r.text(); })
                    .then(function (text) {
                        textEl.textContent = text;
                        modal.style.display = 'flex';
                    });
            });

            document.getElementById('th-license-close').addEventListener('click', function () {
                modal.style.display = 'none';
            });
        })();
    </script>
}
